sdata> -- Issue #69: reaching end-of-input without an explicit QUIT/END exercises a
sdata> -- distinct exit path from repl_dispatch_basic.cmd's QUIT branch -- the
sdata> -- Ada.Text_IO.End_Error handler (Flush_Pager_Buffer + New_Line + exit
sdata> -- REPL), not the Stmt_QUIT/Stmt_END dispatch branch. No QUIT statement
sdata> -- appears below; stdin simply closes after the last line.
sdata> REPEAT 2
sdata> LET X = RECNO
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 2 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> PRINT X
sdata> RUN
1.00000
2.00000
RUN complete. 2 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> 
